From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve MilkDrop mode opacity before volume modulation

Follow MilkDrop 2.25c milkdropfs.cpp:2882-2995,3315-3317: multiply
mode-adjusted alpha by the unbounded volume ramp, replace the mode-3
base alpha with its canvas coefficient, then clamp and skip below .004.
Preserve TV opacity canvas/reference policies, Native dot styles, prepared
geometry replay and patch0014 mode-1 alpha boost. No extra render pass,
texture, sample or persistent equation evaluation is introduced.

Original source: milkdrop2 f05b0d8, milkdropfs.cpp SHA256
68749d31bb6b3020ca89b1e7630fd704e58a5de8dd6275c9f5ea005c6586a7d9.

---
